WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.951
Hook swam toward the pirate boat in the growing darkness.

2
00:00:03.952 --> 00:00:06.996
Starkey held out the lantern to guide him.

3
00:00:06.997 --> 00:00:13.078
Meanwhile, Wendy and Peter were still in the water listening closely to what was happening.

4
00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:16.757
Hook reached the boat and climbed on board.

5
00:00:16.758 --> 00:00:21.911
"Captain, is everything okay?" Smee asked timidly.

6
00:00:21.912 --> 00:00:27.684
All Hook could do was let out a sigh.

7
00:00:27.685 --> 00:00:31.633
"What’s up, Captain?" Smee asked again.

8
00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:35.741
Finally the captain spoke. "The game is over.

9
00:00:35.742 --> 00:00:43.104
Those boys have found a mother to help them." He sighed again.

10
00:00:43.105 --> 00:00:46.031
Wendy felt very proud.

11
00:00:46.032 --> 00:00:50.867
"Oh, what an evil day!" cried Starkey.

12
00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:56.040
"How dreadful! But what’s a mother?" asked Smee.

13
00:00:56.041 --> 00:01:00.279
Wendy was so shocked that she gave out a little yell.

14
00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:04.507
Peter had to pull her under the water to keep her quiet.

15
00:01:04.508 --> 00:01:08.752
Hook heard the noise and said, "What’s that?"

16
00:01:08.753 --> 00:01:14.310
"Nothing but the birds," answered Starkey, raising the lantern.

17
00:01:14.311 --> 00:01:21.400
They could see a nest floating on the lagoon. A big bird sat on top of it.

18
00:01:21.401 --> 00:01:26.119
"See?" said Hook to Smee, pointing to the bird.

19
00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:30.851
"That is a mother. That nest has fallen into the water.

20
00:01:30.852 --> 00:01:33.708
But does the mother desert her eggs?

21
00:01:33.709 --> 00:01:37.787
No! She will sit on them until they hatch.

22
00:01:37.788 --> 00:01:40.889
Then they will become her children.

23
00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:48.880
She protects them from all dangers, like falling into the water or being eaten up by fish."

24
00:01:48.881 --> 00:01:52.912
Hook’s description made the pirates wipe tears from their eyes.

25
00:01:52.913 --> 00:01:58.760
As they watched the mother bird protecting her young, Smee suddenly had an idea.

26
00:01:58.761 --> 00:02:07.878
"Captain," said Smee, "maybe we could kidnap the Lost Boys’ new mother and make her our mother instead."

27
00:02:07.879 --> 00:02:11.756
"What a great idea!" cried Hook.

28
00:02:11.757 --> 00:02:16.131
"We will seize the children and carry them to our ship.

29
00:02:16.132 --> 00:02:19.721
We will make the boys walk the plank.

30
00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:22.944
Then the girl will become our mother!"

31
00:02:22.945 --> 00:02:29.141
"Never!" cried Wendy. Peter had to push her under the water again.

32
00:02:29.142 --> 00:02:34.277
"What was that?" said Hook, trying to listen in the dark.

33
00:02:34.278 --> 00:02:36.636
But everything was quiet now. Then

34
00:02:36.637 --> 00:02:40.737
the captain and his pirates shook hands and hook. They

35
00:02:40.738 --> 00:02:43.254
all swore to the plan. "Yes,

36
00:02:43.255 --> 00:02:52.205
a girl and a mother is just what we need," said Smee, as if he knew all about mothers now. Suddenly,

37
00:02:52.206 --> 00:02:57.316
Captain Hook remembered another girl—Tiger Lily. "Where

38
00:02:57.317 --> 00:03:01.363
is the Indian princess?" he demanded. "We

39
00:03:01.364 --> 00:03:07.037
let her go, just like you told us," said Starkey. "You

40
00:03:07.038 --> 00:03:11.306
let her go?" screamed Hook. "It

41
00:03:11.307 --> 00:03:16.883
was your order. You told us to let her go," said Smee. "That’s

42
00:03:16.884 --> 00:03:20.668
ridiculous! I gave no such order." Realizing

43
00:03:20.669 --> 00:03:26.727
his pirates had been tricked, Hook turned back to the voice he had heard in the dark lagoon. He

44
00:03:26.728 --> 00:03:30.755
yelled out, "Do you hear me?" Though

45
00:03:30.756 --> 00:03:35.097
he knew he shouldn’t answer, Peter couldn’t stop himself. "I

46
00:03:35.098 --> 00:03:41.038
hear you!" he called back, imitating Hook’s voice once again. "Who

47
00:03:41.039 --> 00:03:45.098
are you, stranger?" Hook demanded. Peter

48
00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:51.343
yelled back, "I am Captain James Hook of the Jolly Roger ."

49
00:03:51.344 --> 00:03:57.784
"You are not!" exclaimed Hook. "If you are Hook, who am I?"

50
00:03:57.785 --> 00:04:01.240
"A codfish!" replied the voice.

51
00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:05.945
"A codfish?" said Hook, confused.

52
00:04:05.946 --> 00:04:09.865
Smee and Starkey drew back from their captain.

53
00:04:09.866 --> 00:04:16.692
"Our captain is a codfish? How embarrassing," they said.

54
00:04:16.693 --> 00:04:21.808
Humiliated, Captain Hook decided to challenge the voice.

55
00:04:21.809 --> 00:04:25.516
"Have you got another name?" he called.

56
00:04:25.517 --> 00:04:31.661
Peter could never resist a good game, so he answered, "Yes, I have."

57
00:04:31.662 --> 00:04:35.353
"Is it vegetable?" asked Hook.

58
00:04:35.354 --> 00:04:38.089
"No," Peter answered.

59
00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.020
"Mineral?"

60
00:04:39.021 --> 00:04:40.074
"No."

61
00:04:40.075 --> 00:04:40.871
"Animal?"

62
00:04:40.872 --> 00:04:43.756
"Yes."

63
00:04:43.757 --> 00:04:46.706
"A man?" asked Hook.

64
00:04:46.707 --> 00:04:51.258
"Certainly not!" cried Peter, annoyed.

65
00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:53.095
"A boy?"

66
00:04:53.096 --> 00:04:54.562
"Yes, yes."

67
00:04:54.563 --> 00:04:57.496
"An ordinary boy?"

68
00:04:57.497 --> 00:05:05.108
"No! A very special boy," answered Peter, losing himself in the fun of the game.

69
00:05:05.109 --> 00:05:10.406
"Hmm," said Hook, pretending to be puzzled.

70
00:05:10.407 --> 00:05:15.959
"Can’t you guess?" cried Peter. "Or do you give up?"

71
00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:21.275
"Yes," said Hook eagerly. "I give up."

72
00:05:21.276 --> 00:05:26.281
"I’m Peter Pan!" shouted Peter with great pride.

73
00:05:26.282 --> 00:05:30.678
"Now we have him!" Hook cried gleefully.

74
00:05:30.679 --> 00:05:36.805
"Into the water, Smee and Starkey. Take him, dead or alive."

75
00:05:36.806 --> 00:05:44.576
Hook leapt back into the water.

